# Zero, identity, transpose, conjugate transpose and diagonal trace.
# Shapes are explicit; extensional equality uses the ordinary function rule.

zero_matrix(2,3)(2,3)=0

zero_matrix(2,3) $in matrix(R,2,3)

identity_matrix(3)(2,2)=1

identity_matrix(3)(1,2)=0

identity_matrix(3) $in matrix(C,3,3)

have fn complex_entries(r closed_range(1,2),c closed_range(1,3)) C=r+c+i

transpose(complex_entries,2,3)(3,2)=5+i

conjugate_transpose(complex_entries,2,3)(3,2)=5-i

by fn_extension transpose(transpose(complex_entries,2,3),3,2)=complex_entries

by fn_extension conjugate_transpose(conjugate_transpose(complex_entries,2,3),3,2)=complex_entries

have fn diagonal_entries(r closed_range(1,2),c closed_range(1,2)) R=r+c

trace(diagonal_entries,2)=6

trace(identity_matrix(3),3)=3

forall mat matrix(C,2,3),r closed_range(1,3),c closed_range(1,2):
    transpose(mat,2,3)(r,c)=mat(c,r)

forall mat matrix(R,2,3):
    transpose(mat,2,3) $in matrix(R,3,2)
